WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.530
Esper Roba
Danger of the Psychic Deck

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:37.460
There's a duel over there!

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:41.730
Excuse me.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:48.550
Dinosaur Ryuzaki, my ESP allows me to see all the cards in your hand.

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:53.490
And my Mesmeric Control has put your monster to sleep.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:55.030
How?

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.030
How do you know my hand?

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.630
You're finished, Ryuzaki.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.100
Jinzo attacks!

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:06.100
Psychic Wave!

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.900
My monster!

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:18.050
Even Ryuzaki couldn't do anything!

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.870
His ESP is for real!

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:26.250
Damn!  I couldn't take away a single life point.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.290
I totally lost!

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:33.230
Ryuzaki, give me your rare card and Puzzle Card.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.600
Here!  Take 'em!

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:39.600
Serpent Night Dragon?

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.640
It's an OK card, but I can't use it in my psychic power deck.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:49.250
Who's my next challenger?

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.670
I'll pass.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:56.190
I can't win if you can use ESP to see my cards.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:03.490
How about you?

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.450
Jonouchi, don't do it!

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.250
His name is Esper Roba.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.420
He's a psychic duelist.

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:12.670
Psychic?

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.840
Yeah.  He uses ESP to know our strategies.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:18.810
There's no way you can win.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.720
You really think so?

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.710
Yeah.  It's for your own good.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:23.960
Don't duel him.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:27.580
You really think I can't beat him?

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:28.920
Definitely no!

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.490
Then I'll challenge him!

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:31.260
What?

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:35.690
I promised Yugi that I'll become a true duelist.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.980
Rule #1 in becoming a true duelist:

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.370
Do not turn your back on an opponent!

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:45.440
Rule #2: Duel someone who seems stronger than you!

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:49.390
I don't know if you have ESP, but I'll take you on!

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:51.210
You idiot!  Don't do it, Jonouchi!

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:52.920
Jonouchi?

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:57.700
You're the one who finished second in Duel Kingdom.

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:01.480
Interesting.  I'll duel you.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.290
It seems I've become quite famous.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:07.520
This isn't the time to be happy.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:09.470
He really is an idiot.

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:15.950
Hello?

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:20.040
It's me.  Honda.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.240
Come in.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.830
I brought you something nice.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:25.870
Something nice?

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.540
It's a laptop.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:30.300
I borrowed it from the nurse station.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:35.490
You can watch the duel tournament in Domino City over the internet.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.560
I thought you'd want to see your brother duel.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.040
But I can't see...

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:47.200
I thought I could do the play-by-play for his duel.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.270
Please do so, Honda!

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:53.480
I've never seen my brother duel.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:54.620
I see.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.720
Okay, wait a sec.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.960
What's wrong?

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:06.020
Oops.  I forgot to ask how to use it.

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:11.220
Where did Yugi go?

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.100
There's a rare hunter with a God Card somewhere in this city.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:20.600
For real?

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.450
A duelist with ESP?

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:23.650
Let's check it out!

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:26.520
ESP?

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.300
Just wait, Yugi.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:35.330
I'll win and reach the battlefield where you'll be waiting for me.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.220
Here I go!

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:44.800
Duel!

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.290
My turn!

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:54.170
Nice.  I have pretty good cards.

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:57.100
Jonouchi...

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.980
I found him.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:00.820
Here you go.

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:02.700
Thank you.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.880
Let's see how he's doing.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.040
He's on screen.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.260
Jonouchi, turn one.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.140
The match has just started.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:18.580
I'll play this card-

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.990
I feel the energy of the universe.

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:30.090
I become one with it as it flows through my body.

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:37.040
It is the rule of the universe that I will win the duel right here, right now!

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:41.010
Rule of the universe?  What's he talking about?

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:44.450
I will win.

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:47.880
Stop joking, you psychic freak!

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:49.890
Go, Giltia the D. Knight!

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.070
Disallowed!

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.100
What?  The monster didn't appear!

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:03.900
It is due to his ESP?

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.840
Obey the rules.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.450
An illegal summon?

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.200
What's he doing?

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:17.900
Jonouchi, you idiot!

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:18.750
What?

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.900
That wasn't ESP.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:22.570
It was the card you played!

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:27.120
You can't just bring out a Level 5 monster.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:32.060
You need to tribute a Level 4-or-below monster to summon it.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:35.420
Don't you know the tournament rules?

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:40.000
Oops.  I forgot about tributing.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:43.200
You wasted your turn.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:45.370
I'm giving you a handicap.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:48.380
I'm glad it wasn't ESP.

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:53.860
I'll give you a piece of advice.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:08:02.190
Yes...  Your best move is to play the leftmost card in your hand: Swordsman of Landstar.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:03.370
What?

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:09.400
He read my hand!

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:10.930
It's telepathy.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:12.820
Telepathy?

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:17.300
My heart is one with the all-encompassing universe.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:23.550
As long as we share the same space, I know everything you know.

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:24.980
No way!

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:26.380
My turn!

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:32.120
I summon Cyber Raider!

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:37.610
Attack him directly!

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.330
Cyber Knuckle!

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:49.270
I remember now.

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:55.660
Under Battle City rules, you can attack the opponent directly when he has no monsters on his field.

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:57.450
I end my turn.

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:04.220
He's taking a one-sided beating.

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:06.040
What's wrong with you, Jonouchi?

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:07.520
Honda?

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:10.800
You've been quiet for a while.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:12.820
Is my brother in trouble?

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:15.650
No, it's not that.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:19.200
It's that his opponent is so weak that I feel let down.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:21.870
So my brother is winning?

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.450
Uh, yeah.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:28.480
He's so strong that I want him to go easy on the poor guy.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.340
Thank goodness.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:37.340
C'mon, Jonouchi.  Don't turn me into a liar.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:59.400
Since I heard he used ESP, I thought he'd be Ghouls' rare hunter.  However...

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:07.310
I see a dice card under Swordsman of Landstar.

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:10.420
Big bro, he sees Graceful Dice.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.280
I guess I was wrong.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:30.450
What's wrong?  It's your turn.

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:36.380
Damn.  If I don't summon a monster, he'll attack me directly again.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:40.020
Another Graceful Dice.

00:10:40.210 --> 00:10:41.820
Big bro, can you hear me?

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:44.820
He drew a second Graceful Dice.

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:47.520
Transmitting...

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:50.860
He's doing that again.

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:57.170
You drew a second Graceful Dice.

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:02.490
He's surprised because our bro guessed his card.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:08.080
If Jonouchi is a true duelist, he should figure out this trick.

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:12.030
Are you surprised?

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:15.820
The universe endowed me with telepathic power.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:19.250
It's your turn.  Play a card!

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:25.190
I don't know if he has ESP, but it's clear that he can see the cards in my hand.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:30.620
How can I duel against psychic powers?

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:39.340
Wait, he said that I drew a "second" Graceful Dice.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:41.280
I see!  Maybe he's...

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:42.710
My turn!

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.380
Let's go, Swordsman of Landstar!

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:55.400
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:00.760
Did he set both Graceful Dice cards?

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:06.770
With Graceful Dice, if he has a monster with 500 or fewer attack points...

00:12:06.770 --> 00:12:10.310
...he can roll a die and multiply its attack points by that number.

00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:11.210
I get it.

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:13.700
I know what you're planning!

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:22.540
When my monster attacks, you'll roll the dice to increase Swordsman of Landstar's attack points and strike back!

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:24.000
Who knows.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:28.260
Just watch!  I'm going to debunk your ESP!

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:31.260
But it's pointless to play both cards.

00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:34.700
You can only use one Graceful Dice per turn.

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:39.540
You should restudy the rules.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:41.070
My turn!

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:46.140
I tribute Cyber Raider to summon The Fiend Megacyber!

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:08.830
Now's my chance!  I activate the spell card Graceful Dice!

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:17.560
His monster has 2200 attack points.

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:20.150
My monster has 500 attack points.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:22.410
If I roll a 5 or higher, I can win.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:26.350
You can't win a duel by relying on luck.

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:29.220
Please!

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:33.540
Too bad!

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:37.140
Your monster has 1500 attack points.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:40.230
It's no match for my monster!

00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:43.130
Go!  The Fiend Megacyber attacks!

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:47.430
I trapped you!

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:49.960
I flip over my other set card!

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.940
Hey!  Weren't you listening to me?

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:55.090
You can only play one Graceful Dice per turn-

00:13:55.090 --> 00:13:57.640
I never said it's Graceful Dice!

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:03.950
The spell card Skull Dice?

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:05.650
Impossible!

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:13.230
Skull Dice lowers your monster's attack points based on what I roll.

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:16.450
Oh no!

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:33.150
You thought I had two Graceful Dice, but one of them was Skull Dice.

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:40.820
You mistook one for the other because the two cards were stacked.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:43.260
You could only see the die on one of them.

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:48.520
In other words, it's not ESP that lets you see my hand.

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:52.200
Someone is spying on my hand and informing you!

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:53.300
Gulp!

00:14:53.730 --> 00:14:54.730
What?

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:55.600
Oh no!

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:56.410
He knows!

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:59.400
You figured it out, Jonouchi.

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:02.380
Warning!

00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:04.280
Run!

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:06.290
Stop!

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:12.250
I won't let you escape!

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:15.910
Sorry.  We'll never do it again, so let us go.

00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:20.510
As Battle City commissioner, I can't let this go!

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:23.330
I'll cancel this duel for cheating!

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:24.560
Cancel?

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:25.820
Please don't!

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:29.340
Our big bro is fighting for us!

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:35.780
Our brother resorted to cheating in order to protect us from bullies.

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:38.540
Protect you from bullies?

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:57.830
When our brother started winning duels, everyone stopped bullying us.

00:15:58.150 --> 00:15:59.930
That's why he...

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:02.750
Yugi?

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:09.130
Cheating is cheating!

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:12.510
As commissioner, I won't accept cheating in a duel!

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:16.260
Please!  Let our big brother duel!

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:19.380
Our big bro is really strong.

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:22.880
He can win without cheating if he wants to.

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:30.260
Yugi...

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:32.980
Please!

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:35.020
Let him keep dueling!

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:38.420
Just this one time.

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:41.180
If he cheats again, I won't forgive him.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:42.380
Thank you!

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:44.560
Hooray!

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:47.680
I'm a sucker when it comes to brothers.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:56.680
I can't find him.

00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:06.170
The other Yugi in on his way.

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:10.870
To recover his lost memories.

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:16.170
You say that my ESP is fake?

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:19.210
You shouldn't make false accusations.

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:24.650
I'll use my ESP to predict the future with 100% accuracy.

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:26.350
Predict the future?

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:31.580
I will win this duel, and you will lose!

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:32.720
What?

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:37.560
I can say this because I've never lost a duel.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:40.000
Compared to me, you're an amateur.

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:41.910
Our future is certain.

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:50.220
I can't see the future, but there's someone in this city who's waiting for me.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:56.060
No matter where I'm headed, I know I'll have to duel him.

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:01.250
Jonouchi...

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:05.930
I fight because I believe in this future!  That's all there is to it!

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:09.400
I will destroy that future.

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:14.370
I can beat a duelist like you without communicating with the universe.

00:18:15.050 --> 00:18:16.350
I refuse to lose!

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:20.860
I'll show you how terrifying my psychic cards are!

00:18:20.860 --> 00:18:23.080
Then let's continue the duel!

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:25.850
My turn!

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:30.020
I set a card and end my turn!

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:37.960
Good!  He doesn't have any monsters, so I can attack him directly and damage his life points.

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:40.840
I hope I get a good card!

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:44.730
Nice!  Alligator's Sword!

00:18:45.070 --> 00:18:47.000
I summon Alligator's Sword!

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:53.660
I have two monsters!

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:56.970
Their total attack points equal 3000!  I win!

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:58.410
Here I go!

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:01.750
I attack with two monsters during my Battle Phase!

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:07.650
Alligator's Sword, deal him damage with your Dragon Sword!

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:15.820
Yeah!

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:19.070
Shizuka, Jonouchi will win with one more attack!

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:21.730
Do your best, brother.

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:24.670
Don't lose, big bro!

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:27.340
Don't let your guard down, Jonouchi.

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:30.640
Go, Swordsman of Landstar!

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:32.670
This attack will end the duel!

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:36.080
One can pass, but not the other!

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:38.020
I flip over my trap card!

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:40.340
I activate Mind Control!

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:43.320
Trap card?

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:54.700
The monster caught by this trap become my servant for two turns!

00:19:55.400 --> 00:20:00.570
Why didn't he activate this trap on the first monster?

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:07.250
If he used Mind Control on the first monster and let the two monsters destroy each other...

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:13.530
...Roba could've destroyed all of Jonouchi's monsters without losing any life points.

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:18.460
Since he didn't do that, it means he's going to tribute it!

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:22.370
Go ahead and try.

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:24.650
I'll turn the tables with this card!

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:29.330
I set a card and end my turn!

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:30.860
My turn!

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:36.670
I tribute Swordsman of Landstar to summon Jinzo!

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.610
Jinzo?

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:00.400
Attack me.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:03.630
When you do, Trap Hole of Spikes will destroy it.

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:10.420
It seems you set a trap card, but Jinzo has a special effect.

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:12.700
Trap Crush!

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:17.550
What?

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:23.820
Too bad.

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:28.830
As long as Jinzo is on the field, all your trap cards are destroyed.

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:31.490
He's good...

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:48.960
It's good that Jonouchi figured out Esper Roba's trick, but he's in a pinch again after Roba summons Jinzo.

00:21:49.130 --> 00:21:54.890
Even his special Time Wizard-Baby Dragon combo attack doesn't work against Jinzo?

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:56.760
Don't give up, Jonouchi!

00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:59.710
Shizuka is rooting for you in this duel!

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:05.070
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Courageous Gamble
Spin, Roulette Spider

00:22:05.070 --> 00:22:06.680
Duel, standby!

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:25.960
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:31.330
I feel like I've been here

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:41.010
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:41.310 --> 00:22:52.520
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:55.390 --> 00:23:00.030
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:05.300
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:05.870 --> 00:23:10.410
Will never change

00:23:11.070 --> 00:23:15.680
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:16.310 --> 00:23:20.880
To be who I am

00:23:21.480 --> 00:23:26.120
I've kept searching for something

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:30.830
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:30.830 --> 00:23:33.760
I learned that's the answer

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:40.870
From now until forever...
